  "details": "I'm honestly not sure where its coming from, because on non-ft avatars VRCFT claims its only sending 2 parameters, and the OSC debug screen shows nothing relating to the jaw. And yet on every avatar, even those without ft support, I get jaw tracking as long as the mouth/jaw tracking control is Tracking. \n\nThis would be generally a good thing, however if the avatar *does* have animator-based FT support, then the jaw motion doubles up, causing your jaw to unhinge like a snake. Animator-based FT relies on the tracking control for the mouth remaining tracking so that the visemes still work, since the FT data is not fast enough to fully capture/sync the movement of the lips, so we can't just set the tracking control to Animated.\n\nI also didn't hear anything about this in any of the release notes, it just kind of snuck in I guess? Honestly I like it, and I hope it can be made to work without breaking existing avatars. (Also please fix nothing about it showing up in any of the debug screens).",
